notes = "(!) ROMs go in the RetroArch system folder, or its xroar/ or coco/ subfolder.|(!) Machine defaults to CoCo 3; files in a folder or with a name containing CoCo 1 or CoCo 2 boot a CoCo 2.|(!) Select (remote Channel Down) opens the on-screen keyboard: D-pad moves, B (OK) types, A deletes, Y shift, X moves it, Start enter.|(!) Pad: D-pad/left stick = joystick, B (remote OK) = fire 1, A = fire 2, Start = ENTER, X = 1, Y = 2, L2 = Y, R2 = N.|(!) Disks autorun the program found on them (RUN or LOADM+EXEC)."

description = "XRoar by Ciaran Anscomb, cut down to the Tandy Color Computer 1, 2 and 3. Runs cartridges, cassettes and disks, with autorun."
